Z||000000||Ed||05-23-2001||12:54 AM||||I got rear-ended today.  <P>Some JERK stopped in a traffic lane of one of our busiest streets to look at SOMETHING! and three of us behind him stopped, but another driver DIDN'T!  Then he took off!  Hit and run and four stopped cars damaged, plus the hitter, and he left parts all over the street. Five cars in total.  We had a witness who got a partial plate and car description.<P>I got the worst of it.  Its actually kind of funny.  I rear-ended a Suburban.  You know who won that contest.  My right front is damaged and the hood/deck is broken on that side.  But the funny part is, I hit her trailer hitch receiver on the "Suburban" plug in the square receiver.  So now I have an imprint, backwards, that says Suburban.  My car did (slightly) bend the plug (only). Not the hitch or anything else, only bent the metal plug.  <P>My car's rear is bent, and that's what I think is the worst.  I could see that the frame extension to the "bumper" back there is accordioned, and I can't tell if the engine or suspension frames/mounts are affected.<P>Its just a car, and everyone is okay.  I sure hope the JERK who stopped up front in traffic gets a ticket, and the guy who rear-ended us all gets caught.  <P>Tomorrow the insurance adjuster, and then we'll see if its repaired or replaced.  I already know what (a car already for sale) I'd replace it with if necessary, and if its repaired I'm going to get the whole car repainted.<P>Lemonade out of lemons.<P>Update:  Here's a picture of the damage.  Note the trophies from car shows.  <P>P.S.  I deleted my collision coverage effective ten days ago.  Good timing, huh?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierocrash.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by Ed (edited 05-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-23-2001||09:59 AM||||"Lemonade out of lemons"<P>And thats about all you can do about it too.  As long as you keep your head about yourself, everything will come out right in the end.<P>Just yesterday someone opened their door into my side molding that I have just repainted, and scraped the paint in the exact same spot as someone did last year.  Same size too.  Yes, I was pissed, but, I also have to realize that this is my daily driver car, and crap like that'll happen.  Especially when there are inconsiderate or just plain stupid people.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierodave2001||05-23-2001||10:15 AM||||Wow, sorry to here of the loss. Glad you are okay.<BR>Man what a loser the drive off guy was.<P>Hope he gets nailed.<P>Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Neverfinished||05-23-2001||06:13 PM||||When life gives ya lemons......<BR>Ya mostly end up eating the damn lemons<P>------------------<BR>To Be Old And Wise, You First Must Be Young And Stupid.-----------------<BR>It's not a waste of time... If you are wasted at the time||||reg||10
Z||000004||Formula88||05-23-2001||09:34 PM||||That sucks, man.  I feel your pain, though.  My '99 Grand Am daily driver got front ended (dude in front of me decided to back up to let someone pull into traffic  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> and his trailer bent up the hood on my GA.  Minor damage - I may try to fix it myself.  And I swear, even though I'm paying out the a$$ for this car, the only thing going through my mind was, "Thank god the Fiero didn't get hit!"||||reg||11
